# Force LF line endings on checkout regardless of the puller's core.autocrlf
# setting. Without this, Windows checkouts with autocrlf=true (Git's own
# recommended default there) silently convert LF -> CRLF in tracked text
# files -- git reports no diff (autocrlf normalizes for comparison), but the
# actual working-tree bytes no longer match the committed blob. That broke
# tests/test_generalization_set.py's frozen SHA-256 check on Windows: the
# file content was identical, only the line endings differed.
* text=auto eol=lf
